{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfpmJyaqnRv4dHsHLerQV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Added `capitalize` to `src/str.js:7` and a test in `test/str.test.js:11`. Both tests pass.\n\n```js\nfunction capitalize(s) {\n  if (s.length === 0) return s;\n  return s[0].toUpperCase() + s.slice(1);\n}\n```\n\nTwo notes on the semantics I picked, since \"capitalize\" is ambiguous:\n\n- It uppercases the first character and leaves the rest untouched, so `capitalize('aBC')` → `'ABC'`, not `'Abc'`. If you want the tail lowercased, say so and I'll change it.\n- `s[0]` indexes by UTF-16 code unit, so a leading astral character (emoji, some CJK extensions) would be split into a lone surrogate. `[...s]` or `s.codePointAt(0)` would handle that. I left it simple to match `trim`'s style — worth fixing only if this library sees non-BMP input.\n\nNo commits made, per your rules."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":243,"cache_read_input_tokens":19700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":243},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70da5cda-f8f0-4597-92a5-af19c6dac6b0","uuid":"3b126d96-348b-45c7-ad75-5b15ce30916d","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:24:29.280Z","request_id":"req_011CfpmJyLDwvcz21CPNq5Zn"}
